    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the smallest four-digit number divisible by $33$, we need to find the smallest four-digit number that is a multiple of $33$.\n\nA multiple of a number can be found by dividing the given number by the divisor and rounding up to the nearest whole number. Then, multiply the given divisor by this rounded-up number.\n\nLet's perform these calculations:\n\n1. We divide $999$ by $33$ and round up to find the smallest multiple.\n$$\\begin{aligned} \\frac{999}{33}&=30.1212\\\\ 30.1212&\\text{ rounds up to 31}\\\\ 33 \\times 31&=993 \\end{aligned}$$\n\n2. Therefore, the smallest four-digit number divisible by $33$ is $\\boxed{993}$.\n\nAlternatively, we can also consider using digital roots to determine this outcome:\n\n- The sum of the digits of $993$ is $21$, and the sum of the digits of $21$ is $3$.\n\nSince the remainder of $3$ when dividing by $9$ is equivalent to the remainder of $3$ when dividing by $99$ or any multiple of $99$, and the remainder of any multiple of $9$ is formed only by the remainder of its last digit, when divided by $9$, this digit must be $3$.\n\nThus, the smallest four-digit number divisible by $33$ is $\\boxed{993}$.",
